USAGE
  {{command}} needs [<query>] [--kind <kind>]... [--open] [--color <when>]
  {{command}} needs show <ref> [--color <when>]
  {{command}} needs approve <ref> [--text <markdown> --rev <n>] [--payload <json> --rev <n>] [--confirm] [--yes]
  {{command}} needs answer <ref> [<option>] [--text <answer>] [--yes]

List Needs you, every decision that waits on you in the profile's order, the
queue the cockpit, the menu bar and the floating widget show, or print one
whole: what it asks, its options and the commands it takes. A query narrows it
as the cockpit's lens does (source:github, @context, asked-by:<name>, free
text), and --kind keeps the decisions of a kind (answer, approve-plan,
send-draft, review-step, last-step, pick-someone, act); --open opens the cockpit
on the same queue. Piped, the list is one tab-separated line per item: ref,
kind, task, title, since, primary action and what it asks. An item's ref is its
gate's id; a situation of a unit, which no gate decides, is <kind>@<unit>.
approve resolves an item's gate with its primary action, as the cockpit's button
does; a draft's shows it whole and posts once you say yes at a terminal, from an
agent's shell only with --yes and a session you drive, whose agent asks you
first, and a stale draft is refused; a failed delivery's posts it again. answer
answers a question with one of its options, or your words with --text; an option
that posts a draft shows it and asks first, as approve does.

FLAGS
  --kind <kind>      list: keep the items of this decision kind; repeat it for
                     more
  --open             list: open the cockpit on the same queue, narrowed by one
                     kind at most
  --color <when>     list, show: auto, always or never
  --text <markdown>  approve: post this text instead of the draft's; answer:
                     your answer, after the option when one is given
  --payload <json>   approve: post this payload instead of the draft's, whole
  --rev <n>          approve --text or --payload: the rev of the draft you read,
                     as needs show prints it
  --confirm          approve of a failed delivery: post again a draft that may
                     have been posted
  --yes              approve, answer: go ahead without asking, after showing the
                     draft

EXAMPLES
  {{command}} needs
  {{command}} needs source:github --kind send-draft
  {{command}} needs show 412
  {{command}} needs approve 412
  {{command}} needs answer 398 b
  {{command}} needs @ops --open

DOCS
  https://{{name}}hq.github.io/{{name}}/concepts/home/
